    description: "## What\nA Yjs sync + awareness endpoint on `htrac serve` (Starlette), speaking the y-protocols sync and awareness messages over a WebSocket route beside the existing `/ws` state_snapshot/command channel, serving the projected Y.Doc (item B). Bound to 127.0.0.1 only; the binding is hard-coded, not a flag, until WI-hopip (serve write-API auth) and WI-sunan (tracker self-claims) land.\n## How\n- One room per tracker root. Server side via pycrdt's sync helpers; client side via `y-websocket` 3.1.0 (Yjs 13) or `@y/websocket` (Yjs 14) -- match the ADR's Yjs-version decision.\n- Awareness payload per the ADR: {item_id in view, client label, kind}. Expose \"who is looking at WI-x\" to the TUI/CLI later; for now assert it round-trips between two clients.\n- Alternative acceptable for the first spike: run `npx y-websocket` as a sidecar and have serve only project the doc; record which was chosen.\n## Done when\nTwo browser clients (Playwright) connected to the endpoint converge after concurrent edits to a live-editable field, see each other's awareness, and the endpoint refuses non-loopback binds. serve.py docstring updated. Coverage 100%.\n## Context\n~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/notebookjournal_10162026_2318.md section 4. Security: WI-hopip documents that serve's write API currently has no auth -- this endpoint must not widen that."  # 38a0
    fields: {}  # 38a0
